# WarriorRunAwayPhysicalSpecial (21508) running from the character (i_ai0 1), 200 away, every
# draw 99. The hit that makes the character its most hated, with it holding no effect of skill
# 1201's stack, leaves it running; once the skill lands on it (held), the next hit ends the run
# (i_ai0 3) and drops its walk. The attack weight the held hit leaves is not pinned
# here: tests/ai/warrior_individual5h_test.go asks only that there is one.
character Hunter 20
random always 99
script script.ai.individual.DefaultNpc
script script.ai.individual.Monster.MonsterAI
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.WarriorBase
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.Warrior
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.WarriorRunAwayPhysicalSpecial.WarriorRunAwayPhysicalSpecial
npc runner 21508 Monster 200 0 0 mem i_ai0=1 skill PHYSICAL_SPECIAL 4643 6
roll runner 0

hit runner 10
  mem runner i_ai0=1 c_ai0=player
  effect runner 1201 none
  desires runner attack(player)=125
land runner 1201 1
  effect runner 1201 held
hit runner 10
  mem runner i_ai0=3
